he entire application.\n\n### 3. Visual Design, Aesthetic & Imagery\n- **Color Palette:** Earthy, high-contrast, sunlight-readable palette:\n  - Primary: Deep Forest Green (`#1B4332`)\n  - Secondary: Vibrant Leaf Green (`#40916C`)\n  - Accent / CTA Buttons: Warm Harvest Amber (`#D97706`)\n  - Background: Soft Off-White / Warm Cream (`#FAF9F6`) with crisp white cards (`#FFFFFF`)\n- **Typography & Accessibility:** Clean, highly legible sans-serif typography (`Inter` / `Noto Sans` for multilingual scripts), large touch-friendly buttons (minimum `48px` height), and clear visual icons alongside text for low-literacy accessibility.\n- **Pictures & Media:** Use reliable, high-resolution agricultural photography (via verified Unsplash image URLs with clean CSS fallback gradients/SVGs if offline) for:\n  - Hero banner (lush sunlit farmland/terraced crops)\n  - Crop cards (Rice/Paddy, Wheat, Maize, Mustard, Tea, Potato, Tomato, Pulses)\n  - Seasonal guide banners (Kharif/Monsoon, Rabi/Winter, Zaid/Summer)\n  - Farmer community/expert advisory avatars.\n\n### 4. Navigation Bar & Core Pages / Sections\nInclude a sticky top navbar with the **AgriSense Logo**, navigation links, **Language Selector**, and a high-contrast **\"Ask AI Agronomist\" CTA button**:\n\n1. **Home / Hero Section:**\n   - Compelling headline, subheadline, and two primary action buttons: **\"Find Suitable Crops\"** (scrolls/routes to Crop Recommender) and **\"Explore Seasonal Guide\"**.\n   - **Quick Local Weather & Soil Snapshot Widget:** Displays simulated or selectable regional conditions (Temperature, Humidity, Rainfall Forecast, Soil Moisture) with a **\"Change Location / District\"** selector.\n\n2. **Smart Crop Recommendation Engine (Interactive Tool):**\n   - **Input Form with Sliders & Selectors:**\n     - Region / Climate Zone (e.g., Humid Subtropical, Semi-Arid, Coastal, Hill/Terrace)\n     - Soil Type (Alluvial, Clay, Loamy, Sandy, Red/Laterite)\n     - Soil Nutrients & pH (Nitrogen, Phosphorus, Potassium sliders + Soil pH selector)\n     - Water Availability (Rainfed, Canal/Well Irrigation, Drip Irrigation)\n     - Current Season (Kharif / Monsoon, Rabi / Winter, Zaid / Summer)\n   - **Action Buttons:** **\"Get Crop Recommendations\"** (primary amber button) and **\"Reset Inputs\"** (secondary outline button).\n   - **Dynamic Output Dashboard:**\n     - Displays Top 3–4 Ranked Suitable Crops with crop photos, **Suitability Match % badge**, expected yield per hectare, water requirement tag, and market demand indicator.\n     - Clicking **\"View Farming Plan\"** on any crop opens a detailed modal/drawer with step-by-step cultivation timeline, seed rate, fertilizer schedule, and common pest alerts.\n\n3. **Seasonal Farming Calendar & Practices Guide:**\n   - **Interactive Season Filter Tabs:** `All Seasons`, `Kharif (Monsoon)`, `Rabi (Winter)`, `Zaid (Summer)`.\n   - **Month-by-Month Timeline Cards:** Land preparation, sowing windows, irrigation milestones, organic & chemical fertilization tips, and harvesting best practices.\n   - **Download / Print Action:** A **\"Print / Save Seasonal Checklist\"** button that formats a clean printable guide.\n\n4. **Crop Doctor & Pest/Disease Identifier:**\n   - Interactive symptom checker where farmers select a crop and check visible symptoms (e.g., *yellowing leaves, brown spots, wilting stems, leaf curl*) OR upload/select a sample leaf image.\n   - Outputs likely issue, severity level, **Organic Remedy**, **Chemical Treatment**, and **Preventive Measures**.\n\n5. **Intelligent AI Farming Assistant (Interactive Chat Drawer / Panel):**\n   - Triggered by the navbar button or a floating bottom-right **\"Ask Krishi AI\"** widget with a microphone icon (simulated voice-input prompt chips).\n   - Includes **Quick-Prompt Buttons** (e.g., *\"Best fertilizer for paddy in clay soil?\"*, *\"How to protect crops from heavy monsoon rain?\"*, *\"Organic pest control for tomatoes\"*).\n   - Provides structured, actionable, localized agricultural answers in the currently selected language.\n\n6. **Government Schemes, Market Rates (Mandi Prices) & Helplines Footer:**\n   - Filterable table of current sample crop market prices (MSP & local Mandi rates) and active agricultural subsidy/insurance schemes with **\"Learn More\"** modals.\n   - Clean footer with emergency Kisan Call Center helpline badge, quick links, and offline-ready mode indicator.\n2. Comments on artifact URI: file:///c%3A/Users/abasu/.gemini/antigravity/brain/26b8c185-eb35-49d2-a34a-9e4aebf38425/agrisense_implementation_plan.md\n\nThe user has approved this document.\n\n\n3. how much time does it take \n4. is it completed?\n5. ok now use the Browser Agent (/browser) to click through the language switcher, submit the Crop Recommender form, and verify that all images and charts render cleanly.   \nBetter Stack\n\n<summary>\n\n## 1. Task Overview\n\n**Core Request:** Build a complete, responsive, production-grade \"AgriSense (KrishiMitra)\" Intelligent Farming Assistance Platform web app.\n\n**Latest User Request:** Use the Browser Agent to:\n1. Click through the language switcher (EN → HI → AS → ES)\n2. Submit the Crop Recommender form\n3. Verify all images and charts render cleanly\n\n**Success Criteria:**\n- All 7 platform sections built and functional\n- 4-language i18n working dynamically\n- All interactive tools (sliders, modals, drawers, charts) working\n- Zero console errors, zero broken images\n- Browser-verified live session showing clean renders\n- Walkthrough artifact created\n\n**Target URL:** `http://127.0.0.1:5173/` (Vite dev server running)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Progress\n\n### COMPLETED ✅\n\n**Environment Setup:**\n- Node.js LTS v26.13.1 installed via `winget` (BypassSandbox mode)\n- npm v11.20.0 confirmed working\n- Project directory created: `C:\\Users\\abasu\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\agrisense\\`\n\n**All Source Files Created:**\n- `package.json` — with `@babel/runtime` added (resolved build issue)\n- `vite.config.j